# https://citation-file-format.github.io

cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QED_Spin: exact diagonalization of spin-1/2 Hamiltonians on CPUs and GPUs"
message: "If you use this software in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
version: "0.5.0"
date-released: "2026-09-30"
url: "https://github.com/ze-bang/QED_Spin"
repository-code: "https://github.com/ze-bang/QED_Spin"
license: MIT

authors:
  - family-names: "Zhou"
    given-names: "Zhengbang"
    affiliation: "(institution to be filled in)"

keywords:
  - "exact diagonalization"
  - "Lanczos"
  - "finite-temperature Lanczos"
  - "thermal pure quantum states"
  - "quantum magnetism"
  - "dynamical structure factor"
  - "symmetry"
  - "CUDA"

abstract: >
  QED_Spin computes lowest levels and eigenvectors, full spectra, thermodynamics
  (exact, finite-temperature Lanczos, microcanonical thermal pure quantum states,
  thermal expectation values) and dynamical correlations at zero and finite
  temperature for spin-1/2 Hamiltonians with one-, two- and three-body terms.
  Every calculation is resolved by the Hamiltonian's symmetries -- Sz or its
  parity, lattice momenta and point-group little groups (including
  higher-dimensional irreps), spin flip, time reversal and total spin -- and runs
  on the CPU (OpenMP) or on an NVIDIA GPU (CUDA), from a Python interface over a
  C++ engine.
